  message: "Measurement 0009 (WI-vapud) re-derived this item's mechanism from the opposite direction and put a volume on it inside the ADR-0049 family. The discriminator is sharper than 'method rows need a typed receiver': a receiver typed from a CONSTRUCTOR or a DECLARED PARAMETER resolves, and a receiver typed from an external function's RETURN VALUE does not resolve at all. Measured, two languages, controlled within the same fixture: go -- 'var r gin.Engine; r.Run()' FIRES, 'r := gin.Default(); r.Run()' emits dst_ref module=None; java -- 'Socket s = new Socket(h,p); s.getInputStream()' FIRES, 'Connection c = DriverManager.getConnection(u); c.prepareStatement(s)' emits dst_ref module=None. Java also types a receiver from a declared parameter (EntityManager em -> em.getReference fires), which is why the java arm looks partly healthy. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE ADR-0049 RETAG: all seven go third-party framework launch rows (gin.Engine.Run/RunTLS, fiber.App.Listen/ListenTLS, echo.Echo.Start/StartTLS, grpc.Server.Serve) are INERT in real code, because every one of those frameworks is entered through a constructor call -- gin.Default(), fiber.New(), echo.New(), grpc.NewServer(). Plus java.sql.Connection.prepareStatement/prepareCall. Those nine rows are the concrete near-term payoff of this item, and until it lands they are the rows INV-kanuk should retag LAST. Fixtures: idiom/gofull and idiom/javafull in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/vapud_reach_08292026/."  # 8fd0
